WEBVTT

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.240
Yahoo!

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.020
I just love my
RZV 500R!

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.560
It was definitely worth blowing
my savings on this!

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:11.030
I'll get Miyuki to do a little more monkey-
wrenching and it'll be perfect! Hmm?

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.760
Oh no, it's starting
to rain!

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.410
<i>Wrong gear!</i>

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.420
<i>I'm not gonna</i>
<i>make it!</i>

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.020
<i>My RZV! My hard-earned</i>
<i>bonus money!</i>

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.680
What are you sighing
about?

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.440
Problems with
your love life?

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.250
No, guess it wouldn't be.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.480
It is.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.090
Someone wants me to consider
an omiai introduction.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.080
What?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.820
A neighbor said it's time I should
be thinking about marriage.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.820
She's made plans to introduce
me to someone.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:51.050
But she's been very nice to me, so
I can't tell her I'm not interested.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.300
Yeah? Which
is it?!

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.130
Pardon?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.330
The person she's introducing you
to. Is it a man, or a woman?

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.560
A man.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.140
Unreal!

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:05.640
What do you think I
should do? Hmm?

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:10.710
This is scandalous! Talk about great
gossip! How avant-garde!

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.090
Excuse me...

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.750
Marvelous!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.810
What?!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.580
You're kidding!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.260
What's the point of trying
to fix it? It's totaled!

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.860
I'm counting on you!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.300
Who is to blame for taking it out like
that, especially on racing slicks?

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.260
Hmm?

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.800
And who was it that took it out without
bothering to change the brake pads?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.030
That was... uh...
Here's a 14mm.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:39.800
I told you not to take it out until
I'd finished working on it.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.040
But I wanted
to, so bad!

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.980
You're just lucky you
weren't hurt.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.050
For the time being, you're
not allowed to ride.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.390
What?! Not even the mini-bike?

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:51.880
No.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.290
Not even in the city?

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.230
'Course not.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.960
That's not fair!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.930
Why not use a car, like the rest of us?

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:58.720
Huh?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.730
You did go to the trouble of
getting a license, after all.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.300
So how about getting a car this time?

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.770
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.800
Maybe I should
get a car.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.310
Tsujimoto's gonna
buy a car?!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.810
Don't you think you're
overreacting a little?

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.550
You should reconsider this!

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.060
We don't need more work!

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.750
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.830
It's too dangerous!

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.290
No way!

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.420
Are you nuts?!

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:33.160
Have you even thought of the
safety of the local people?!

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.530
Now that hurts.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.040
Maybe you shouldn't go through with this.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.670
Not you too, Chief?!

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.360
Why's that?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.510
Because!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.790
<i>"Shift gears! Now!"</i>

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.080
"Not quite!"

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.590
<i>"There!"</i>

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.360
<i>"Uh... the brake!</i>
<i>Brake!"</i>

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:11.300
She wouldn't drive a car any differently
than she drives a motorbike.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.840
Most of the acceleration
in two gears...

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.640
...engine brake for
slowing down...

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.540
...looking left and
right for safety...

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.620
...it's all the same whether
it's a bike or car!

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.280
No way!

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:33.320
<i>"Anyway, you only live once,</i>
<i>so don't rush into this."</i>

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.830
I can't believe even the
Chief won't back me.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.450
I really do want a car now.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.850
Hello.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.810
Are you looking for something
in particular?

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:00.280
Who, me?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.920
Hey!

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.190
<i>Natsumi?!</i>

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.440
I can't believe you found
a Subaru R2!

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:24.900
Right! They're
hard to find.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:29.540
So the nice salesman told me I should
snatch it up while I had a chance.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.680
It has power steering and power windows!
Not to mention a power-assist clutch!

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.590
I've never heard of an R2 with
power steering before.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.490
Hmm? The door
won't open.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.630
Sure it will!
It's easy!

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:49.230
See? Oops.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.730
Maybe I put too much
muscle behind it.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.770
Look at this, it's filthy inside!
Wow! This is so hard!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.340
The window and the clutch are manual!
They're way too sticky!

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.710
And what's with this handle
for the window?

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:07.120
I thought it was supposed
to be a power window?!

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.280
This is ridiculous!

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.150
What kind of power steering, power
windows, and clutch are these?!

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.200
This window takes
power!

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:27.670
And this clutch is a
great leg workout!

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.610
Isn't that what "power"
means?

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:36.080
So that's what you've thought
for the past 20 years?

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:43.590
This whole car is falling apart.
And it's covered in rust.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.360
Where'd you buy this thing?

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.860
Kato's Used Cars.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:47.880
Really?

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:52.260
I thought that place had a good reputation.
I haven't heard anything bad about them.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.600
Oh well, I guess you could either get them
to fix it or ask to trade for another car.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:03.110
Boy, this power steering really
does take a lot of power!

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.110
lmpossible.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.100
Why?

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.810
Because this car never
came from our lot.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:10.880
What?

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.150
Look at this.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.550
Your receipt is different
from ours.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.120
No way!

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.860
The guy who sold it to me gave me
a business card and everything.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.630
See?

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:29.000
Just as I suspected. It's
different from ours.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.870
And we don't have anyone
here named Akutoku.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.370
He was a fraud.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.850
But he was so kind.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.850
Who?

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.580
The salesman.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:50.120
He asked if it was
my first car.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:55.060
I don't know anything about cars, but he
was all smiles, explaining everything.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.960
He didn't seem like
a con man.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:03.970
I should have listened
to the Chief.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.110
It's green, Natsumi.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:19.050
It won't start.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.220
Natsumi.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.500
Still having problems
with being fixed up?

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.200
Yes. I can't put it off. She
even gave me his picture.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.860
What?! Let's see!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:47.580
Woo-hoo! What a man! Maybe
I need to get fixed up, too.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.820
Don't buy impulsively. You'll
regret it if you do.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.870
Natsumi.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.930
Okay. I'll give
it a go.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:27.090
What are you going to do?

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.610
Just wait and see.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:34.520
The guys at the lot said they'd find the
parts, so it should work out fine.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.830
Let me take care of it, and don't worry.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.270
Don't put yourself out over this.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:39.890
What?

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:43.130
If I hadn't gone out and bought
it without thinking...

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:45.970
...I wouldn't have been tricked
by that con man.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.270
Natsumi.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:12:00.480
Maybe I just wasn't meant
to have a car.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.820
Hi. Where are
you off to?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.590
The cafeteria.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.660
What's eating
her?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.560
She's worse than
I thought.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.300
Chief!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.200
Chief!
It's hurt her pride, as a cop.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.870
She won't forgive herself for letting
someone con her like that.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.430
Happens all
the time.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:30.810
Chief, can't you try to cheer her up
or something? I'm sure it'd work!

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:35.850
Hmm. There's something that'd
work better, right over there.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.330
You're right!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.080
<i>You just wait,</i>
<i>Natsumi.</i>

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.940
<i>I'm going to use everything I've got</i>
<i>and build you a very special bike.</i>

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.710
<i>There won't be another R2</i>
<i>like it in the entire world!</i>

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:12.290
<i>Yeah. I'll get Yoriko and Nakajima</i>
<i>to help me out, too.</i>

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.410
Yeah, all right there...

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:43.760
Oh!

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.490
Hard at it, huh?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.760
Daimaru! And Mr. Kanno!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.330
It's been awhile.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:52.160
Here's the chain and sprocket you wanted.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.400
Thanks a lot! You didn't have
to bring it over in person!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:00.570
I couldn't believe you were going to
do all that customizing to the R2.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.680
You surprised me!

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.270
You're a remarkable young woman.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.650
Well, I had to do it for Natsumi.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:08.200
Hmm?

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:14.280
I keep thinking, "Natsumi would do it this
way". Or, "Natsumi would like it like this."

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:15.910
I'm having fun just
planning it.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:21.480
I see. You must be very close, to have
such a clear idea of what she likes.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.300
You're a remarkable woman!

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.470
That was my line!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.400
Huh?!

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:43.540
Natsumi.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.240
Huh? What's this?

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.110
Well?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.710
"Well?!" Is this
my R2?

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:17.780
Looks completely different, huh?

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.150
Unreal!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.820
Wow!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.720
Hey, Miyuki. What's this thing
hanging out the back?

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:31.260
Give it a kick,
Natsumi.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.200
A kick?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:37.760
Yeah, at the back left. It's a kickstarter.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.470
Uh... I see.
I found it.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:47.250
All right, kick away.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.040
Here goes.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.190
That sound...

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.330
My bike.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:18.810
Yes. I used all the bike parts I could find.
And a chain instead of the drive shaft.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:24.750
You put the 2-cycle, V4 engine
from my RZV in this car?

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.350
The gears are
sequential.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:32.220
You push ahead for the first gear,
and pull it back for 2, 3 and 4.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.150
It's the same
as a bike!

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:38.530
You have to keep it above
4,000 rpm, too.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.770
Thank you, Miyuki. Thank you!

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.500
Aha! It's alive!

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:47.300
Natsumi's RZV!

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.560
Huh? What's
this?

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.840
You're right! It's
back in action.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:59.820
Huh? Hey, Kobayakawa.
I found out where he is.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.420
Let's go get him.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:03.320
Who?

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:12.830
When we took it apart, the serial numbers
of the chassis and engine didn't match.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.300
He sure goes
pretty far.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:19.030
This car was assembled with stolen parts
and parts from cars in accidents.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.710
I see.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.830
We all got together...

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:27.040
...and tracked down who's been
buying up parts for the R2.

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:30.310
What's the
address?

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:35.350
What kind of
car is that?!

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.120
This is the
place.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.520
His name is Shin'ichi Aida.
Lives on the fourth floor.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.560
According to the
neighbors...

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.540
...he seems like a kind,
good young man.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.980
Excuse me ladies, but
I'd like to get out.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:25.140
Don't floor it like that! The chain'll break!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.570
I know, I know!

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:33.940
As if your stupid little patrol
car can stop my Camry!

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:38.220
I'm not going to be beaten by a Camry.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:43.050
Sounds weird. He's really souped it up.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:49.060
A wolf in sheep's clothing, huh? He
probably used stolen parts, too.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.190
I'll unmask him.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.740
Natsumi!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.740
What?!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.540
It's not a bike! You can't turn by leaning!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.970
Oh, no! That's a hard
habit to kick!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.480
My beautiful
paint job!

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.290
I learn from my mistakes!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.850
What the hell?

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:23.790
Shin'ichi Aida, stop the
car! You can't escape!

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.100
You're a fraud!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.940
I know what you're
all about!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.450
The door!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.440
No!

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.450
<i>You can't</i>
<i>beat me.</i>

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:49.590
I won't let you
beat me!

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:50.880
Feel the mortal blow...

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:54.390
...of my power kick!

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.230
You're a monster!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.710
I've oversteered!

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.100
So, what's going on with that
guy you were fixed up with?

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:45.470
What? Oh that...
Well, uh...

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:48.410
What's the matter? Why don't
you make up your mind?

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.480
He's awfully good-
looking!

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.660
Well, I found out he's a marriage con man.

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.020
What?!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.790
My poor neighbor was so shocked
she got ill. Poor lady.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:06.720
It just goes to show that you can't judge
someone by their appearance.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.990
You are living
proof of that.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.000
Lucky for
you...

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:16.970
...the seat belt and air bag
saved your life.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:24.710
I don't believe it. How could a junky
R2 corner so well, or go so fast?

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.590
You taught me a lesson.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.240
What?

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:33.520
Whether it's people or cars, you just
can't judge by appearances.

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:42.600
Cars just aren't my
thing, I guess.

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:47.170
Maybe you're right. Bikes are
probably more up your alley.

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:31.240
I'm tellin' you as is, there's not
much that we can do 'bout it!

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:35.340
You mean, just 'cuz we're dealing
with an idol star?!

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:37.250
Well, what can I say...

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:42.080
Ch... Chief! I can't believe I heard
your mouth say those words!

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:45.020
Next time, You're Under Arrest, File 33...

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:46.730
..."Wow! Catching an Idol Star."

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:49.860
Just you wait, idol man!
